{
  "_comment": "LoopStar input FX presets (Phase LI, iPhone). What the mic or instrument goes through on its way into a loop: you hear it while you play (headphones), and it is printed into the take. Fields, all optional (absent = off): compression 0-1; drive {style: lofi|crush|speaker|funk|overdrive|highgain, mix 0-100}; pitch semitones -12..12; eq {low, mid, high} dB -12..12; delay {beats (quarter-note beats: 0.75 = dotted eighth), feedback 0-90, mix 0-100}; reverb {space: room|chamber|plate|hall|cathedral, mix 0-100}. Delay is ALWAYS a note value -- it follows the tempo (../LOOPSTAR_SOUL.md). Edit or add here; zero rebuild. INPUT TYPES (2026-10-15, the board's pedals): `inputTypes` groups presets by what is plugged in or played; a type lists preset ids in order, `icon` is an SF Symbol name. A preset may sit in several types. OUR OWN PEDALS (2026-11-17): amp {model (an amps.json id), cab (a cabinet id; absent = the amp's own), gain, bass, mid, treble, level 0-1; knobs left out = the amp's defaults}; wah {mode pedal|auto, position 0-1, sensitivity 0-1}; mod {type chorus|phaser|tremolo, beats (a note value, quarter-note beats), depth 0-1 (tremolo: shape), mix 0-100 (tremolo: depth)}. comp {style: warm|glue (amps.json pedals.comp.styles), amount 0-1} (2026-11-18): LoopStar's own compressor instead of the plain `compression`.",
